{"agent":"pa2-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`fsio.rmtree_owned` raises `ValueError` (empty, relative, cwd, or filesystem root) and can also raise from `Path.resolve()` (symlink loop), while the previous `shutil.rmtree(..., ignore_errors=True)` did not raise. That call sits in a `finally` after `return rehearsal.run(), rehearsal`. If `work` is `Path('')`, `Path('.')`, `Path.cwd()`, or `Path('/')`, or `resolve()` fails, the `finally` exception discards a successful return and replaces whatever `rehearsal.run()` raised, so the dry-run result never reaches the caller.","digest":"1b63eb171746ae3e","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/upgrade_dryrun/_drive.py:27","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/upgrade_dryrun/_drive.py:27"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The surrounding handler is documented as never raising: a failed removal must be left for `cleanup` to name and prune, and this handler is the only cleanup. `fsio.rmtree_owned(tree)` raises `ValueError` before `ignore_errors` applies. Given `tree` equal to `Path('.')`, `Path('')`, `Path.cwd()`, or `Path('/')` (plausible if the process’s cwd is the worktree being torn down), the handler raises and the later `worktree prune` does not run.","digest":"df72c55b2731305a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:73","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py:73"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The loop’s next line treats a refused removal as non-fatal (`if not old.exists()` then it is not recorded). `rmtree_owned(old)` does not return on refusal; it raises. One relative doomed path (for example `Path('.ddflow/backups/old-tag')` when the repo root was not made absolute) or a path that resolves to the cwd aborts the sweep, so later doomed trees are not removed and the function does not return the removals already done.","digest":"14df0a173c79d646","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/backups.py:113","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/backups.py:113"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12552,"diff_sha":"383debc30e2a85176f3cc0015f77fcfbb8f4b74c9dea8136833de7d1b303e992","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/AU-safe-rmtree","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":141.7,"family":"xai","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"0c48a9963a40926c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/AU-safe-rmtree.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T043127Z-d21e76fd.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"a92336091d169f4755e932538f344c1ec304ada3","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/infra/fsio.py":"100644 0d58749fe8ba54bdcc5464c34d7a155f1edd7046","ddflow/infra/worktree/_create.py":"100644 12f8934b66d436089a552838bf4a8da877ba40af","ddflow/services/backups.py":"100644 a00983d1215176c395cd5d24d2ba97c711e59e49","ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py":"100644 46e19626fa3ad6dfe466002d556c30f0d60069c9","ddflow/services/cleanup/actions.py":"100644 6d66d04448bafbdf69a48773366e5c0d4fb2ab64","ddflow/services/lane_headless.py":"100644 4aac3029e75cfefe509cd12f1afbb2f06cdc6ccf","ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks.py":"100644 fa37e28c2d1fb66265e622b609906ebd04138f3f","ddflow/services/upgrade_dryrun/_drive.py":"100644 392a0e3d16139493847e30eb3d532c4b65cd644d","ddflow/services/upgrade_dryrun/_steps.py":"100644 94850a26c0f6a44a1994f0f7ac4430dd71890499","tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.ci.scratch.toml":"","tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.cleanup.actions.toml":"","tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.upgrade_dryrun._drive.toml":"","tests/test_rmtree_owned.py":"100644 4a65b931bfa04ab46d702065f401f491429e8510"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","revie