{"agent":"pa2-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`rmtree_owned` always calls `p.resolve()` and `Path.cwd().resolve()` before it consults `ignore_errors`, and it does not catch the errors those calls raise. Given an absolute owned target such as `Path('/tmp/legit-tree')` with the default `ignore_errors=True`, if the process cwd has been unlinked, `Path.cwd()` raises `FileNotFoundError` and the tree is never removed. The same leak happens when a path component is not a directory (`NotADirectoryError` from `resolve()`) or is a symlink loop. Callers that previously used `shutil.rmtree(..., ignore_errors=True)`, including the scratch handler documented as never raising, now abort and skip later cleanup.","digest":"5637afe4f974de21","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/infra/fsio.py:rmtree_owned","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/infra/fsio.py:rmtree_owned"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`test_refuses_an_empty_path_silently_by_default` only asserts `Path.cwd() == tmp_path` after `fsio.rmtree_owned(\"\")`. The failure mode the module docstring names is that `shutil.rmtree('', ignore_errors=True)` empties the cwd (children gone, directory inode still there), so cwd identity is unchanged and this assertion still holds. With a marker file in `tmp_path`, an unfixed call that deletes that marker still passes, so the test does not fail against the unfixed code the change claims to regress.","digest":"61208d0725e90a8e","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_rmtree_owned.py:22","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_rmtree_owned.py:22"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":13472,"diff_sha":"0cac7a19ab352fb7cdf4ce23446c4abf4f9966d993d56b9e76c51cda12b1d828","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/AU-safe-rmtree","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":